What the long lived people of Okinawa can teach us about a reason to get up in the morning.
---PAGE---
# What it is about

Two writers visit Ogimi, a Japanese village famous for its centenarians, and ask what keeps people active and content into old age. They find purpose, friendship, gentle movement, modest meals and work that never quite stops. A short, calm, illustrated read.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Ikigai is the overlap of what you love, what you are good at, what the world needs and what you can be paid for.

Staying lightly busy matters more than retiring; many of the villagers never fully stop working.

Small daily rituals, close friends and eating until you are almost full add up over decades.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For anyone wanting a gentle, quick read about purpose rather than a programme to follow.

