# What it is about

In nineteen short chapters, Morgan Housel shows that financial outcomes are driven less by spreadsheets than by ego, fear, patience and luck. Stories replace formulas, and the advice is modest: save, stay in the game, and know what is enough.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Wealth is what you do not see: the money not spent on looking rich.

Compounding rewards time more than brilliance, so the first job is simply to avoid being wiped out.

Everyone\'s view of money is shaped by their own slice of history, which is why reasonable people disagree.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For first time savers and investors who want principles they will still agree with in twenty years.

