A Nobel laureate\'s tour of the two systems in your head, and how often the fast one fools you.
---PAGE---
# What it is about

Daniel Kahneman describes a quick, intuitive System 1 and a slow, effortful System 2. Through decades of experiments he shows how the fast system produces confident errors in judgement, from anchoring to overconfidence, and what little can be done about it.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Most decisions are made by fast intuition, with slow reasoning stepping in less often than we think.

Losses hurt roughly twice as much as equal gains please, which bends our choices.

We judge by what comes to mind easily, so vivid stories beat dull statistics.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For patient readers who enjoy evidence and are willing to doubt their own judgement.

