Copying takes the world from one to many. Creating something new takes it from zero to one.
---PAGE---
# What it is about

Based on a class Thiel taught at Stanford, this short book argues that the most valuable companies build something genuinely new instead of competing in crowded markets. It is opinionated, contrarian and full of questions founders should ask.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Competition erodes profit; lasting businesses find a small market they can dominate first.

Ask what important truth very few people agree with you on. Good companies are built on such secrets.

Start small, then expand step by step, rather than chasing a huge market from day one.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For anyone curious about startups who prefers arguments to checklists.

