# What it is about

Eric Ries applies lean manufacturing ideas to new ventures. Instead of long plans and big launches, he proposes small experiments, honest metrics and a willingness to change direction. The vocabulary he introduced is now standard in the industry.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

A minimum viable product is the smallest thing you can build to learn something real.

Vanity metrics flatter; actionable metrics tell you whether to persevere or pivot.

The build, measure, learn loop should run as quickly as possible.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For founders, product teams and students working on a project nobody has asked for yet.

