People do not buy what you do. They buy why you do it.
---PAGE---
# What it is about

Simon Sinek looks at leaders and companies that inspire loyalty and finds they communicate from the inside out: purpose first, then method, then product. He calls the pattern the Golden Circle and argues it can be learned.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

The Golden Circle runs from why, to how, to what, and most organisations explain it backwards.

A clear purpose attracts people who share it, which is stronger than any incentive.

Success can blur the original why, so it has to be restated as an organisation grows.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For team leaders, club committees and anyone who has to persuade others to care.

