# What it is about

Susan Cain examines how Western culture came to prize the outgoing personality, and what is lost when quieter people are overlooked. Drawing on psychology and many interviews, she argues for workplaces and classrooms that make room for both temperaments.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Introversion is about where you get your energy, not about shyness.

Group brainstorming and open offices often produce worse ideas than time alone.

Quiet leaders can do especially well with teams that take initiative.
