  (36, 'BNT-000136', '9780807014271', 'Man\'s Search for Meaning', 'Viktor E. Frankl', 'Beacon Press', 'Paperback', 6, 'A psychiatrist\'s account of surviving the camps, and what kept people alive inside them.', 'Viktor Frankl describes his years in Nazi concentration camps and what he observed there as a psychiatrist. In the second part he outlines logotherapy, his view that the deepest human drive is the search for meaning. Short, sober and unforgettable.', '# About this preview

Man\'s Search for Meaning is still in copyright, so BookNest does not show pages from the book itself. This short preview was written by our librarians to help you decide whether it is for you.

A psychiatrist\'s account of surviving the camps, and what kept people alive inside them.
---PAGE---
# What it is about

Viktor Frankl describes his years in Nazi concentration camps and what he observed there as a psychiatrist. In the second part he outlines logotherapy, his view that the deepest human drive is the search for meaning. Short, sober and unforgettable.
---PAGE---
# Three ideas you will meet

Those who held on to a purpose were more able to endure.

We cannot always choose our circumstances, but we can choose our response to them.

Meaning is found in work, in love and in the stance taken toward unavoidable suffering.
---PAGE---
# Is it for you?

For anyone going through a hard time, and everyone else too.

